nd Removing Disparate Impact.\" *Proceedings of the 21th ACM SIGKDD International Conference on Knowledge Discovery and Data Mining*, 259–268. [Techniques for detecting and mitigating disparate impact.]\n- Hardt, M., Price, E., & Srebro, N. (2016). \"Equality of Opportunity in Supervised Learning.\" *Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems*, 29. [Formalization of equality of opportunity.]\n- Kleinberg, J., Mullainathan, S., & Raghavan, M. (2016). \"Inherent Trade-Offs in the Fair Determination of Risk Scores.\" *arXiv preprint arXiv:1609.05807*. [Impossibility results for fairness metrics.]\n- Kotsiantis, S. B., & Kanellopoulos, D. (2006). \"Disparity Detection in Credit Scoring Using Artificial Neural Networks.\" *Proceedings of the 10th WSEAS International Conference on Computational Intelligence*, 315–320. [Early work on disparity detection in risk scoring.]\n- Mullainathan, S., & Obermeyer, K. (2017). \"Predicting Patients in the Emergency Department: A Machine Learning Approach.\" *Proceedings of the 23rd ACM SIGKDD International Conference on Knowledge Discovery and Data Mining*, 547–555. [Application of ML to public benefit contexts.]\n- Pedregosa, F., et al. (2011). \"Scikit-learn: Machine Learning in Python.\" *Journal of Machine Learning Research*, 12, 2825–2830. [Standard ML library used for model implementation.]\n- Shalev-Shwartz, S., & Ben-David, S. (2014). *Understanding Machine Learning: From Theory to Algorithms*. Cambridge University Press. [Theoretical foundation for generalization and distribution shift.]\n- Zemel, R., Wu, Y., Swersky, K., Pitassi, T., & Dwork, C. (2013). \"Learning Fair Representations.\" *Proceedings of the 30th International Conference on Machine Learning*, 325–333. [Approaches to learning representation-invariant models.]\n\n---\n\n*End of Proposal*\n",
